melody:
# Chorus (as in the Public Domain Song Anthology, from the 1906 edition)
You're a grand old flag, you're a high-fly-ing flag, and for-ev-er in peace may you wave;
D5/ B4/ G4 G4 G4 E4/ D4/ G4/ A4 F#4/ G4 E4/ D4/ G4 E4/ D4/ G4 E4/ D4/ A4(2) ~A4/ r/
you're the em-blem of the land I love, the home of the free and the brave.
D4/ E4/ F#4 G4 A4. D4/ G4 A4 B4. G4/ A4/ B4 G4/ A4/ B4 G4/ A4(2) ~A4/ r/
Ev-'ry heart beats true un-der Red, White and Blue, where there's nev-er a boast or brag;
D5/ B4/ G4 G4 G4 E4/ D4/ G4/ A4 F#4/ G4 F#4/ F4/ E4 G#4/ B4/ E5 D5 C5(2) r
but should auld ac-quaint-ance be for-got, keep your eye on the grand old flag.
D4/ D4/ G4. F#4/ G4 B4 A4. G#4/ A4 D4/ D4/ E4/ G4 E4/ G4 A4 G4 r r

